lid` and literal member-specific details. Add one admitting narrowing per site to the shipped harness and show each new named test kills its narrowing alone with raw logs. Then update the gate × entry census, TRACEABILITY, and measured AC ratio. Keep the orchestrator-approved `byte_counts` stated bound and the unchanged production behavior unless a new test exposes a real defect. This is one `to-dev` rework cycle for the single mechanism, not a separate research or harness task.\n79|\n80|Free hunt found no other blocking mechanism. No surface row was omitted.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ed","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0cfdc-90e4-7130-b73f-3760c218f2ff"},"sequence":337,"recorded_at":1780531400000669,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65e49a74-cdff-4e0c-a0aa-7ac50dfdd8b5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"65e49a74-cdff-4e0c-a0aa-7ac50dfdd8b5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65e49a74-cdff-4e0c-a0aa-7ac50dfdd8b5"},"call_id":"call_01a0cfdd5481703ca42749636e0f2f2d","text":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-2ya5le/rev2read/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2ya5le Results — implement-fidelity-report-and-reason-registry (rev2 rework)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-21bxa3`, tip `0ca3e4c`);\n5|no commit on the Story branch. This is the FIRST leaf of\n6|STORY-260830-21bxa3; the Change Request is `task_delta` (no\n7|registry edit — the Story's final leaf carries it).\n8|\n9|Rev2 answers review verdict rev1 (`unbound-byte-aggregate`,\n10|CHANGES REQUESTED) per the orchestrator rework decision: pinned\n11|SPEC v0.7.0 §13.14.2 lists `byte_counts` as a \"closed map of every\n12|disposition to uint53\" that must \"reconcile exactly to the rows\"\n13|(lines 10636/10645), but `FidelityDispositionRecord` carries no\n14|byte measure — the only byte measure in §13.14 is\n15|`CaptureItem.byte_count` in §13.14.1 (line 10471), on the Capture\n16|Manifest, and the spec defines no byte basis for canonical-event\n17|or synthesized rows. That is a gap in the specification, not a\n18|defect closable by inference, and guessing bytes from digests or\n19|row counts is forbidden. Decision: `byte_counts` is\n20|shape-validated in this leaf and carried as an explicit STATED\n21|BOUND. \"The DoD item on aggregates is satisfied by the decision\n22|above.\" Rev2 delta vs rev1 is exactly three non-production files\n23|(verified byte-identical production via the rev1 CR patch: all 10\n24|production files identical): the `TestByteCounts` rename into an\n25|explicit bound witness, two harness killer-name strings, and two\n26|TRACEABILITY rows. Zero production bytes changed.\n27|\n28|Authority: the task record's v0.5.0 §13.14.2/§13.14.4 is STALE per\n29|the brief. All behavior is pinned to `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n30|§13.14.2 \"Fidelity, projection, and lineage\" (line 10548+), quoted\n31|in code comments and tests. §13.14.4 carries no constraint on the\n32|report shape (verified by read: it references only the\n33|`fidelity_report_id` digest in events) — sibling scope.\n34|\n35|## What was built\n36|\n37|New package `internal/clonefidelity` (6 production files):\n38|\n39|- `vocab.go` — the four closed registries: 7 dispositions, 5\n40|  profiles, 5 strategies, 19 core reasons + reverse-DNS extensions\n41|  (`ValidDisposition`, `ValidProfile`, `ValidStrategy`,\n42|  `ValidReasonCode`, `IsCoreReasonCode`, list accessors).\n43|- `record.go` — `FidelityDispositionRecord` build/decode with the\n44|  four record rules (exact⟺empty reasons; non-exact≥1;\n45|  synthesized⇒null canonical; evidence presence for all rows).\n46|- `report.go` — `BuildFidelityReport` / `DecodeFidelityReport` for\n47|  the closed 29-member Fidelity Report 1.0.0: branch-exact\n48|  archive/target nullability, row ordering (source sorted, then\n49|  synthesized sorted, keys unique), derived counts/reason counts,\n50|  closed 26-kind / 8-type breakdowns reconciled per disposition,\n51|  closed 7-key byte map, policy map, and omit-self identity.\n52|- `decode.go`, `errors.go`, `doc.go` — delegated parse helpers,\n53|  `ErrInvalid` refusal identity, authority/reuse/bounds doc.\n54|\n55|Landed-owner touch (reviewed diff: +67/−1, purely additive):\n56|\n57|- `internal/clonebundle`: `CheckExtensionsClosed`,\n58|  `EncodeExtensions`, `OmitSelfDigest`, `EventKinds`,\n59|  `ContentBlockTypes`, `ValidContentBlockType` — one-line delegates\n60|  over tested internals.\n61|- `internal/environ`: `CheckReverseDNS` (new) + `CheckExtensions`\n62|  refactored onto it (one line, behavior-identical).\n63|\n64|Nothing else changed. No README/doctor/config surface (a library,\n65|not a command); no registry edit; no sibling contract.\n66|\n67|## AC coverage: 39 of 40 rows driven + 1 stated bound\n68|\n69|`TASK-260830-2ya5le_conformance-matrix.md` (attached): 40 AC rows,\n70|39 driven through a production entry by a named committed test;\n71|every gate row carries a directly-reddening narrowing (§A). The\n72|35-test suite (333 pass lines incl. subtests) is green with 97.1%\n73|statement coverage. The one stated bound is row 24,\n74|byte-aggregate reconciliation: `byte_counts` values are\n75|shape-validated only (exact seven-disposition keys + uint53 —\n76|keys + values gated, bound witnessed by admission over identical\n77|rows), because no row-reconciled byte invariant is expressible\n78|until the spec defines a byte basis for canonical-event and\n79|synthesized rows. Owner: spec clarification\n80|(agent-session-manager-spec) + the §13.14.1 capture-manifest\n81|leaf. Rows 33–36 are admitted properties / cross-checks with no\n82|gate to narrow (disclosed, not waived). Nothing here claims\n83|`byte_counts` is row-reconciled.\n84|\n85|Key enumerations (oracles retyped from spec text, never imported):\n86|\n87|- Vocabularies: 7 + 5 + 5 + 19 members admitted; 24 + 17 + 15 + 27\n88|  refusal tokens plus empty plus 5 non-strings each refused with\n89|  literal codes; core/extension disjointness asserted per core code.\n90|- Record grid: 7 × {0,1,2,128,129} × canonical × evidence = 140\n91|  cells through both entries (35 admit / 105 refuse, first-fire\n92|  literals asserted).\n93|- Aggregates: counts 14-cell ±1 sweep; reason 6-cell sweep +\n94|  extra/missing/zero keys; event-kind 182-cell +1 sweep + 7 −1;\n95|  content-block 56-cell +1 + 7 −1; byte keys/values + 6 bad shapes.\n96|- Identity: test-side JCS recompute agrees