{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca35","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0cfdc-90e4-7130-b73f-3760c218f2ff"},"sequence":885,"recorded_at":1780531400001765,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65e49a74-cdff-4e0c-a0aa-7ac50dfdd8b5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"65e49a74-cdff-4e0c-a0aa-7ac50dfdd8b5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65e49a74-cdff-4e0c-a0aa-7ac50dfdd8b5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0cfe1-9b92-71c2-842c-c5b6b47583ff"},"task_id":"01a0cfe1-9b92-71c2-842c-c5b6b47583ff","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0cfe1-9b92-71c2-842c-c5b6b47583ff","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonefidelity/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-2ya5le)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonefidelity`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Section 13.14.2 \"Fidelity,\n5|projection, and lineage\" (line 10548+). This is the FIRST leaf's\n6|clause record for the fidelity-projection-and-validation-contracts\n7|story; record clause-to-test bindings here. The\n8|`internal/traceability` registry edit belongs to the Story's final\n9|leaf, not this one.\n10|\n11|## Why this package exists\n12|\n13|Section 13.14.2 states the disposition, reason, profile, and\n14|strategy vocabularies, `FidelityCounts`,\n15|`FidelityDispositionRecord`, the Fidelity Report 1.0.0 closed table,\n16|and the reconciliation rules that follow it. No landed package owns\n17|them: the `canonicaljson` closed-shape registry recognizes\n18|`urn:ax:schema:fidelity-report` only to refuse it\n19|(`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape`, pinned by that table's\n20|census), so this package is the validating owner. Sibling leaves\n21|own Projection Plan, Read-Back, Validation Report, Migration\n22|Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt; where the report references them,\n23|only the identity or digest field is carried.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Strict JSON framing | `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` at `decodeStrictObject`: the report, every row, every counts record, and every map member refuse lone-surrogate escapes, duplicate members, non-objects, and trailing data before any member is read |\n30|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every bound, both entries |\n31|| String/uint53/digest/UUID bounds | `internal/environ` | `CheckStringBounds`, `CheckUint53Bounds`, `CheckDigest`, `CheckUUIDv7` at every decode site |\n32|| Sorted-unique arrays | `internal/environ` | `CheckSortedUniqueStrings`, `CheckSortedUniqueDigests` at every decode site |\n33|| Reverse-DNS grammar | `internal/environ` | `CheckReverseDNS` (new export; `CheckExtensions` refactored onto it with identical behavior) behind extension reasons |\n34|| Environment Tuples | `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeTuple` at both tuple members, both entries |\n35|| Canonical bytes, digests, UUIDs | `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar` | `Canonicalize`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseDigest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n36|| Closed extension values | `internal/clonebundle` | `CheckExtensionsClosed` (new export) at both extension members on decode; `EncodeExtensions` (new export) on build |\n37|| Omit-self digest | `internal/clonebundle` | `OmitSelfDigest` (new export) behind `verifySelfDigest` |\n38|| Event kinds (26) | `internal/clonebundle` | `EventKinds()` iterated for the closed key set; `ValidEventKind` in tests |\n39|| Content-block types (8) | `internal/clonebundle` | `ContentBlockTypes()` (new export) iterated for the closed key set; `ValidContentBlockType` (new export) in tests |\n40|| Capture classes (9) | `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` for `required_dispositions` keys |\n41|\n42|The six `clonebundle`/`environ` exports are additive one-line\n43|delegates over tested internals; no behavior in those packages\n44|changed (importer grid in the conformance matrix,\n45|`clonebundle`/`environ` suites green before and after).\n46|\n47|## Interpretation record (decided, pinned)\n48|\n49|These readings are taken where the pinned text underdetermines the\n50|gate. Each is pinned by a named test, not prose.\n51|\n52|| # | Reading | Test |\n53||---|---|---|\n54|| I1 | `required_dispositions` keys are the 9 capture classes: the spec word for a closed class vocabulary is \"capture-class\" (kinds are \"kinds\", block types are \"types\") | `TestRequiredDispositions` (all 9 admit; `user_message` refused as a key) |\n55|| I2 | `event_kind_counts`/`content_block_counts` carry exactly all 26/8 keys; per-disposition cross-sums equal the row-derived counts (the reconciliation expressible without per-row kind/block fields) | `TestEventKindBreakdown`, `TestContentBlockBreakdown` (closed keys + 182/56-cell +1 sweeps + non-zero -1 cells) |\n56|| I3 | `forbid_reasons` admits literal bounded strings: the table row types them as strings, not reason codes | `TestForbidReasons` (`frobnicate` seals and decodes) |\n57|| I4 | `required_dispositions` values are 1..7 by set semantics (sorted-unique over 7 dispositions); no separate upper check | `TestRequiredDispositions` |\n58|| I5 | Non-synthesized rows admit a digest or null `canonical_object_id`: capture items that never normalized carry null | `TestRecordGridOracle` (non-synth/null-canonical cells admit) |\n59|| I6 | Every row carries `source_evidence_ids[1..65536]` (shape bound for all rows, including synthesized) | `TestRecordGridOracle` (absent-evidence cells refuse on every disposition) |\n60|| I7 | \"A target report does not name Clone Validation Report, Lineage Receipt, G4, or a future event\" holds structurally: the closed 29-member set has no such member | `TestReportMemberSet` (unknown member refused) |\n61|| I8 | Row order is source rows sorted by key, then synthesized rows sorted by key, keys unique across all rows | `TestRowOrdering` |\n62|\n63|## Clause map\n64|\n65|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n66||---|---|---|\n67|| 13.14.2 seven dispositions admitted exactly | `ValidDisposition`, `BuildFidelityReport`, `DecodeFidelityReport` | `TestDispositionVocabularyOracle` (7 admit + predicate/build/decode; 24 refusal tokens + 5 non-strings refuse with the literal code) |\n68|| 13.14.2 five profiles admitted exactly | `ValidProfile`, `BuildFidelityReport`, `DecodeFidelityReport` | `TestProfileVocabularyOracle` (5 admit; 17 refusals + 5 non-strings) |\n69|| 13.14.2 five strategies admitted exactly | `ValidStrategy` (registry entry; no report field carries a strategy) | `TestStrategyVocabularyOracle` (5 admit; 15 refuse) |\n70|| 13.14.2 nineteen core reasons + reverse-DNS extensions; extensions can never redefine a core code | `ValidReasonCode`, `IsCoreReasonCode`, both report entries | `TestReasonVocabularyOracle` (19 core + 5 extensions admit; 27 refusals + empty + 5 non-strings refuse; disjointness asserted per core code), `TestReasonShadowImpossible` |\n71|| 13.14.2 `FidelityDispositionRecord` exact 11-member shape | `DecodeFidelityReport` → `decodeDispositionRecord` | `TestRecordMemberSet` (unknown + 11 missing) |\n72|| 13.14.2 exact requires empty reasons; non-exact requires ≥1 | `checkRecordReasonRule` (both entries) | `TestRecordGridOracle` (140 cells through both entries; 35 admit, 105 refuse with first-fire literals) |\n73|| 13.14.2 synthesized requires no source canonical object | `checkRecordCanonicalRule` (both entries) | `TestRecordGridOracle` |\n74|| 13.14.2 non-synthesized rows trace to source evidence | shape bound + stated resolution bound | `TestRecordGridOracle` (presence half); resolution bound below |\n75|| 13.14.2 record string bounds at edge/edge+1, character measure | both entries via `environ.StringLength` | `TestRecordFieldBounds` (9 refusal pairs + edge admission + null locator), `TestRecordMultibyteMeasure` (512/513 `é`) |\n76|| 13.14.2 sorted-unique arrays (unsorted + duplicate) | both entries | `TestRecordSortedUnique` (4 arrays × 2 shapes × 2 entries) |\n77|| 13.14.2 Fidelity Report exact 29-member set, schema/version literals | `DecodeFidelityReport` | `TestReportMemberSet` (unknown + 29 missing + 9 literal cases), `TestReportRoundTrip` (wire literals) |\n78|| 13.14.2 `fidelity_report_id` is the JCS digest omitting only itself | `BuildFidelityReport`, `verifySelfDigest` | `TestReportIdentityIndependent` (test-side JCS recompute agrees; omitting scope instead disagrees; tampered claim and non-digest refuse) |\n79|| 13.14.2 archive/target branch-exact nullability | both entries | `TestArchiveTargetBranches` (10 build flips + 10 decode flips + profile/scope coupling 5×2×2) |\n80|| 13.14.2 rows ordered, synthesized after source | `checkRowOrder` (both entries) | `TestRowOrdering` (5 build + 5 decode violations) |\n81|| 13.14.2 `counts` derived from rows | `deriveCounts`, both entries | `TestCountsDerived` (literal totals + 14-cell ±1 sweep + zero-cell uint53 boundary) |\n82|| 13.14.2 `reason_counts` derived from rows | `deriveReasonCounts`, both entries | `TestReasonCountsDerived` (literal occurrences incl. shared reason + 6-cell sweep + extra/missing/zero keys) |\n83|| 13.14.2 `event_kind_counts` closed map reconciled | `decodeBreakdown`/`buildBreakdown` + `checkBreakdownSums` | `TestEventKindBreakdown` (182-cell +1 sweep + 7 non-zero -1 + closed keys + build-side rows) |\n84|| 13.14.2 `content_block_counts` closed map reconciled | same | `TestContentBlockBreakdown` (56-cell +1 sweep + 7 non-zero -1 + closed keys + build row) |\n85|| 13.14.2 `byte_counts` closed seven-disposition map | `decodeByteCounts`/`buildByteCounts` | `TestByteCountsReconciliationIsAStatedBoundUntilSpecDefinesByteBasis` (exact keys, uint53 values, 6 bad-value shapes; value reconciliation is the explicit stated bound below, witnessed by admission) |\n86|| 13.14.2 `required_dispositions` closed policy map | `decodeRequiredDispositions`/`buildRequiredDispositions` | `TestRequiredDispositions` (9 classes admit, empty map admits, 6 build + 8 decode refusals) |\n87|| 13.14.2 `forbid_reasons` sorted unique strings | both entries | `TestForbidReasons` (literal strings kept, 128/129 edges, 4 build + 6 decode refusals) |\n88|| 13.14.2 row cardinality [1..1000000] | `checkRowCount` (both entries) | `TestRowCountEdges` (0/1/1000001 at the entries) + `TestCheckRowCountEdges` (999999/1000000/1000001 at the factored gate) |\n89|| 13.14.2 evidence/attestation bounds at edge/edge+1 | both entries | `TestEvidenceBounds` (65536 admit ×3 + 64 admit; 65537/65 refuse both entries) |\n90|| 13.14.2 scalar gates (digests, UUIDv7, tuples) | both entries via landed owners | `TestScalarGates` (15 build + 18 decode rows) |\n91|| 13.14.2 AX number model (no fractions/exponents/strings/≥2^53) | decode via `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` | `TestNumberModel` (4 cells × 7 bad values + max admit) |\n92|| 13.14.2 closed extensions (reverse-DNS keys, AX values, no nested dup) | both entries via `clonebundle` owner | `TestExtensionsClosed` (admission + 6 build + 4 decode rows) |\n93|| 13.14.2 strict framing (dup/trailing/non-object/surrogate/UTF-8) | `decodeStrictObject` | `TestReportFraming` (5 report + 1 row rows) |\n94|| 13.14.2 build UTF-8 pre-marshal gate | build string admissions | `TestBuildUTF8` (key/explanation/reason/extensions) |\n95|| 13.14.2 determinism (identical inputs, identical bytes) | `BuildFidelityReport` | `TestReportDeterminism` (10 builds byte-identical) |\n96|| 13.14.2 purity (no durable write) | both entries | `TestEntriesArePure` (input bytes untouched) |\n97|| 13.14.1 owner vocabularies equal the spec lists | `clonebundle` tables iterated by production | `TestOwnerVocabulariesMatchSpec` (26/8/9 cross-checks + own registry counts) |\n98|\n99|## Durability\n100|\n101|This package holds no local state and performs no durable write:\n102|sealing is pure bytes (`json.Marshal` + JCS + SHA-256 over memory),\n103|so crash semantics are vacuous. The durability proof is\n104|determinism plus purity: `TestReportDeterminism` (ten builds\n105|byte-identical) and `TestEntriesArePure` (decode never mutates its\n106|input; every build output decodes clean).\n107|\n108|## Mutants\n109|\n110|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 62 narrowing rows plus the\n111|harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Every narrowing weakens\n112|one gate to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject,\n113|and every killer drives a production entry. Shared gates (one\n114|implementation, two call sites: the vocabulary predicates, the\n115|reason/canonical/order/count helpers, the breakdown sums, the\n116|row-count gate, the strict frame) carry one plant each with a\n117|dual-entry killer, exactly like the prior leaf's `N-strict-*` rows;\n118|rules implemented twice (build + decode) carry one plant per side.\n119|`N-disposition-route` and `N-reason-core-route` are the\n120|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for token still matches\n121|while the decision changes, and the killers execute the behavioral\n122|oracle suites through both entries. `N-rowcount-max` and\n123|`N-rowcount-min` are the factored-bound narrowings (the exact edges\n124|are pinned at the factored gate; entry reachability by\n125|`TestRowCountEdges`). `N-record-synth-canonical` is labelled\n126|single-member class. The battery runs twice with one raw log per\n127|plant per run carrying the subprocess exit.\n128|\n129|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n130|\n131|- Cross-artifact row coverage (\"every Capture Manifest item and\n132|  Canonical Event occurs in exactly one non-synthesized row\") needs\n133|  the manifests as inputs; no entry in this leaf takes them.\n134|- Source-evidence resolution (rows trace to captured bytes) needs\n135|  the Capture Manifest; only ID presence/shape is gated here.\n136|- `byte_counts` value reconciliation is an EXPLICIT STATED BOUND\n137|  (AC 39 of 40 driven + 1 bound): rows carry no byte measure and\n138|  the spec defines no byte basis for canonical-event or synthesized\n139|  rows, so only the exact seven-disposition key set and uint53\n140|  values are gated (witnessed by\n141|  `TestByteCountsReconciliationIsAStatedBoundUntilSpecDefinesByteBasis`\n142|  admission of differing bytes over identical rows). Owner: spec\n143|  clarification (agent-session-manager-spec) + the §13.14.1\n144|  capture-manifest leaf.\n145|- The core-derived booleans admit any value except the pinned\n146|  archive rule (both target booleans false for archive).\n147|- Per-row target evidence (`target_locator`, staged/live arrays) in\n148|  archive scope is admitted as shaped; no scope-based row refusal is\n149|  pinned in the spec text.\n150|- `forbid_reasons` admits literal bounded strings (I3), not\n151|  reason-vocabulary members.\n152|- Admission at exactly 1,000,000 rows is pinned at the factored\n153|  `checkRowCount` gate plus entry reachability rows, not by sealing\n154|  a million-row report (see `TestRowCountEdges` and\n155|  `TestCheckRowCountEdges`).\n156|- Sections 13.14.3-13.14.5 and the Projection Plan, Read-Back,\n157|  Validation Report, Migration Checkpoint, and Lineage Receipt\n158|  contracts are sibling scope: this leaf plans no projection,\n159|  stages no target, and carries only identity/digest references.","final_result":true}}}
